.nh
.TH "LAGO" "1" "Aug 2026" "Lago CLI" "Lago CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
lago-coupons-update - Update a coupon


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlago coupons update  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
This endpoint is used to update a coupon that can be then attached to a customer to create a discount.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--amount-cents\fP=""
	The amount of the coupon in cents. This field is required only for coupon with 'fixed_amount' type.

.PP
\fB--amount-currency\fP=""
	The currency of the coupon. This field is required only for coupon with 'fixed_amount' type.; one of: , AED, AFN, ALL, AMD, ANG, AOA, ARS, AUD, AWG, AZN, BAM, BBD, BDT, BGN, BIF, BMD, BND, BOB, BRL, BSD, BWP, BYN, BZD, CAD, CDF, CHF, CLF, CLP, CNY, COP, CRC, CVE, CZK, DJF, DKK, DOP, DZD, EGP, ETB, EUR, FJD, FKP, GBP, GEL, GIP, GMD, GNF, GTQ, GYD, HKD, HNL, HRK, HTG, HUF, IDR, ILS, INR, ISK, JMD, JPY, KES, KGS, KHR, KMF, KRW, KYD, KZT, LAK, LBP, LKR, LRD, LSL, MAD, MDL, MGA, MKD, MMK, MNT, MOP, MRO, MUR, MVR, MWK, MXN, MYR, MZN, NAD, NGN, NIO, NOK, NPR, NZD, PAB, PEN, PGK, PHP, PKR, PLN, PYG, QAR, RON, RSD, RUB, RWF, SAR, SBD, SCR, SEK, SGD, SHP, SLL, SOS, SRD, STD, SZL, THB, TJS, TOP, TRY, TTD, TWD, TZS, UAH, UGX, USD, UYU, UZS, VND, VUV, WST, XAF, XCD, XOF, XPF, YER, ZAR, ZMW

.PP
\fB--applies-to-billable-metric-codes\fP=""
	An array of billable metric codes to which the coupon is applicable. By specifying the billable metric codes in this field, you can restrict the coupon's usage to specific metrics only.

.PP
\fB--applies-to-plan-codes\fP=""
	An array of plan codes to which the coupon is applicable. By specifying the plan codes in this field, you can restrict the coupon's usage to specific plans only.

.PP
\fB--code\fP=""
	Unique code used to identify the coupon.

.PP
\fB--coupon-type\fP=""
	The type of the coupon. It can have two possible values: 'fixed_amount' or 'percentage'.
.IP \(bu 2
If set to 'fixed_amount', the coupon represents a fixed amount discount.
.IP \(bu 2
If set to 'percentage', the coupon represents a percentage-based discount.; one of: fixed_amount, percentage

.PP
\fB--description\fP=""
	Description of the coupon.

.PP
\fB--expiration\fP=""
	Specifies the type of expiration for the coupon. It can have two possible values: 'time_limit' or 'no_expiration'.
.IP \(bu 2
If set to 'time_limit', the coupon has an expiration based on a specified time limit.
.IP \(bu 2
If set to 'no_expiration', the coupon does not have an expiration date and remains valid indefinitely.; one of: no_expiration, time_limit

.PP
\fB--expiration-at\fP=""
	The expiration date and time of the coupon. This field is required only for coupons with 'expiration' set to 'time_limit'. The expiration date and time should be specified in UTC format according to the ISO 8601 datetime standard. It indicates the exact moment when the coupon will expire and is no longer valid.

.PP
\fB--frequency\fP=""
	The type of frequency for the coupon. It can have three possible values: 'once', 'recurring' or 'forever'.
.IP \(bu 2
If set to 'once', the coupon is applicable only for a single use.
.IP \(bu 2
If set to 'recurring', the coupon can be used multiple times for recurring billing periods.
.IP \(bu 2
If set to 'forever', the coupon has unlimited usage and can be applied indefinitely.; one of: once, recurring, forever

.PP
\fB--frequency-duration\fP=""
	Specifies the number of billing periods to which the coupon applies. This field is required only for coupons with a 'recurring' frequency type

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for update

.PP
\fB--input\fP=""
	Complete JSON request body or @file.json

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	The name of the coupon.

.PP
\fB--percentage-rate\fP=""
	The percentage rate of the coupon. This field is required only for coupons with a 'percentage' coupon type.

.PP
\fB--reusable\fP=""
	Indicates whether the coupon can be reused or not. If set to 'true', the coupon is reusable, meaning it can be applied multiple times to the same customer. If set to 'false', the coupon can only be used once and is not reusable. If not specified, this field is set to 'true' by default.


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	Override the Lago API key

.PP
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	Override the Lago API URL

.PP
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	Confirm a dangerous operation with its resource identifier

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Print mutating requests without sending them

.PP
\fB--insecure\fP[=false]
	Allow insecure HTTP or TLS for self-hosted Lago

.PP
\fB--mode\fP=""
	Environment mode: live or test

.PP
\fB--no-retry\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic retries

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="table"
	Output format: table, json, or yaml

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	Named profile to use

.PP
\fB--query\fP=""
	JMESPath expression applied to the response

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	Total request timeout

.PP
\fB--timing\fP[=false]
	Print request latency breakdown

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	Print redacted request and response details


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  lago coupons update <code> --input @payload.json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBlago-coupons(1)\fP
